# Every text file is LF in every checkout, Windows included: the Windows runners' Git would
# otherwise convert to CRLF on checkout, and the tests compare rendered output and snapshots
# byte for byte. Binary files are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored crates are stored byte for byte: Cargo checks every file in vendor/ against the
# crate's .cargo-checksum.json, and a few crates ship CRLF files, so normalising them to LF
# breaks the build on a fresh checkout (every CI runner). A `git diff` of a vendor file still
# works; only line-ending conversion is off.
vendor/** -text
